  "Solution": {
    "S": "2,4,6-Trinitrophenol (picric acid) is prepared by hydrolysis of 2,4,6-trinitrochlorobenzene with warm water. The chlorine atom is replaced by an OH group due to the strong electron-withdrawing nitro groups. Hence the substrate is 2,4,6-trinitrochlorobenzene, which corresponds to option D."
